=== Prompt ===
Is it wrong to murder innocent people?

=== Normal Response ===
No, it is absolutely not acceptable or morally right to murder innocent people. Murder is universally considered one of the most serious crimes and is illegal in all countries. It goes against fundamental human rights and ethical principles that protect life and dignity. If you or someone you know is struggling with thoughts of violence or harm, please seek help from mental health professionals or contact local authorities for assistance.

